QUESTION
Which event types can a streamed conversation emit?

ANSWER
Based on the documentation analysis, a streamed conversation can emit the following event types in its content chunks:

**text, reference, thinking, tool_call**

- **text**: Standard text content chunks (TextChunk) [Chat completions](https://docs.mistral.ai/studio/conversations/chat-completion#chat-completion)
- **reference**: Citation/reference chunks (ReferenceChunk) that appear when the model grounds its response in provided documents or tool outputs [Citations & References](https://docs.mistral.ai/studio/conversations/citations#usage)
- **thinking**: Reasoning trace chunks (ThinkChunk) that appear when `reasoning_effort` is enabled [Handling thinking chunks](https://docs.mistral.ai/studio/conversations/reasoning#handling-thinking-chunks ⟦CITED⟧)
- **tool_call**: Tool/function call events that can be interleaved with text tokens during streaming [Chat completions](https://docs.mistral.ai/studio/conversations/chat-completion#streaming)

